Location></itemProps><coordRef><type Sync="TRUE">Geographic</type><geogcsn Sync="TRUE">GCS_WGS_1984</geogcsn><csUnits Sync="TRUE">Angular Unit: Degree (0.017453)</csUnits><peXml Sync="TRUE">&lt;GeographicCoordinateSystem xsi:type='typens:GeographicCoordinateSystem' xmlns:xsi='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance' xmlns:xs='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema' xmlns:typens='http://www.esri.com/schemas/ArcGIS/3.0.0'&gt;&lt;WKT&gt;GEOGCS[&amp;quot;GCS_WGS_1984&amp;quot;,DATUM[&amp;quot;D_WGS_1984&amp;quot;,SPHEROID[&amp;quot;WGS_1984&amp;quot;,6378137.0,298.257223563]],PRIMEM[&amp;quot;Greenwich&amp;quot;,0.0],UNIT[&amp;quot;Degree&amp;quot;,0.0174532925199433],AUTHORITY[&amp;quot;EPSG&amp;quot;,4326]]&lt;/WKT&gt;&lt;XOrigin&gt;-400&lt;/XOrigin&gt;&lt;YOrigin&gt;-400&lt;/YOrigin&gt;&lt;XYScale&gt;11258999068426.238&lt;/XYScale&gt;&lt;ZOrigin&gt;-100000&lt;/ZOrigin&gt;&lt;ZScale&gt;10000&lt;/ZScale&gt;&lt;MOrigin&gt;-100000&lt;/MOrigin&gt;&lt;MScale&gt;10000&lt;/MScale&gt;&lt;XYTolerance&gt;8.983152841195215e-09&lt;/XYTolerance&gt;&lt;ZTolerance&gt;0.001&lt;/ZTolerance&gt;&lt;MTolerance&gt;0.001&lt;/MTolerance&gt;&lt;HighPrecision&gt;true&lt;/HighPrecision&gt;&lt;LeftLongitude&gt;-180&lt;/LeftLongitude&gt;&lt;WKID&gt;4326&lt;/WKID&gt;&lt;LatestWKID&gt;4326&lt;/LatestWKID&gt;&lt;/GeographicCoordinateSystem&gt;</peXml></coordRef></DataProperties><SyncDate>20260120</SyncDate><SyncTime>10222100</SyncTime><ModDate>20260122</ModDate><ModTime>16023400</ModTime><scaleRange><minScale>150000000</minScale><maxScale>5000</maxScale></scaleRange><ArcGISProfile>ISO19139</ArcGISProfile></Esri><dataIdInfo><envirDesc Sync="TRUE">Microsoft Windows 10 Version 10.0 (Build 26200) ; Esri ArcGIS 13.0.0.36056</envirDesc><dataLang><languageCode value="zho" Sync="TRUE"/><countryCode value="CHN" Sync="TRUE"/></dataLang><idCitation xmlns=""><resTitle Sync="TRUE">AUT_Roads</resTitle><presForm xmlns=""><PresFormCd value="005" Sync="TRUE"/></presForm><date><createDate>2026-01-15T00:00:00</createDate><pubDate>2026-01-22T00:00:00</pubDate><reviseDate>2026-01-22T00:00:00</reviseDate></date></idCitation><spatRpType><SpatRepTypCd value="001" Sync="TRUE"/></spatRpType><idPurp>The purpose of this dataset is to model the spatial accessibility and network impedance of the Austrian road infrastructure under simulated flood conditions (HQ30 and HQ100). By integrating hydrological hazard extents with transportation attributes, the layer enables the calculation of dynamic travel times, accounting for the significant reduction in vehicular and pedestrian velocity when road segments are submerged. It serves as the backbone for evacuation route optimization, allowing emergency planners to identify "bottlenecks" where critical infrastructure intersects with flood zones and to estimate the realistic time-window available for residents to reach the nearest safety hubs or shelters.</idPurp><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;This layer provides a high-resolution representation of the Austrian road network, enriched with flood-impact attributes derived from 30-year and 100-year return period hazard maps. Unlike static road datasets, this layer incorporates a dynamic velocity model: while dry segments maintain a standard evacuation speed of 5km/h, segments identified as "flooded" (via spatial intersection with ) are assigned a severely degraded speed of Is_flood30/100&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;0.5km/h to simulate the physical resistance and hazards of moving through water.The dataset allows for advanced "Service Area" and "Closest Facility" analyses within a GIS environment. By comparing dry-state versus flood-state travel times (), the analysis exposes areas of "Sudden Isolation"—communities that may be geographically close to shelters but become functionally unreachable once the road network is compromised. This spatial logic corrects the common misconception that proximity to safety equals security, emphasizing that infrastructural permeability is the true determinant of successful horizontal evacuation.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</idAbs><idCredit>PLUS</idCredit><searchKeys><keyword>road</keyword><keyword>Austria</keyword><keyword>isflooded</keyword></searchKeys><themeKeys xmlns=""><keyword>Is_flooded,Travel time,road, Austria, isflooded</keyword></themeKeys><dataExt xmlns=""><exDesc>WGS84,Deg</exDesc><geoEle xmlns=""><GeoBndBox><westBL>9</westBL><eastBL>18</eastBL><southBL>46</southBL><northBL>50</northBL></GeoBndBox></geoEle></dataExt><tpCat><TopicCatCd value="005"/></tpCat><tpCat><TopicCatCd value="007"/></tpCat><tpCat><TopicCatCd value="016"/></tpCat></dataIdInfo><mdLang><languageCode value="zho" Sync="TRUE"/><countryCode value="CHN" Sync="TRUE"/></mdLang><mdChar><CharSetCd value="004" Sync="TRUE"/></mdChar><distInfo xmlns=""><distFormat xmlns=""><formatName Sync="TRUE">Shapefile</formatName><formatVer>1.0</formatVer></distFormat><distTranOps xmlns=""><transSize Sync="TRUE">0.000</transSize></distTranOps></distInfo><mdHrLv><ScopeCd value="005" Sync="TRUE"/></mdHrLv><mdHrLvName Sync="TRUE">dataset</mdHrLvName><refSysInfo><RefSystem><refSysID><identCode code="4326" Sync="TRUE"/><idCodeSpace Sync="TRUE">EPSG</idCodeSpace><idVersion Sync="TRUE">6.2(3.0.1)</idVersion></refSysID></RefSystem></refSysInfo><spatRepInfo><VectSpatRep><geometObjs Name="AUT_Roads"><geoObjTyp><GeoObjTypCd value="002" Sync="TRUE"/></geoObjTyp><geoObjCnt Sync="TRUE">0</geoObjCnt></geometObjs><topLvl><TopoLevCd value="001" Sync="TRUE"/></topLvl></VectSpatRep></spatRepInfo><spdoinfo><ptvctinf><esriterm Name="AUT_Roads"><efeatyp Sync="TRUE">Simple</efeatyp><efeageom code="3" Sync="TRUE"/><esritopo Sync="TRUE">FALSE</esritopo><efeacnt Sync="TRUE">0</efeacnt><spindex Sync="TRUE">FALSE</spindex><linrefer Sync="TRUE">FALSE</linrefer></esriterm></ptvctinf></spdoinfo><eainfo><detailed Name="AUT_Roads" xmlns=""><enttyp><enttypl Sync="FALSE">Polyline</enttypl><enttypt Sync="TRUE">Feature Class</enttypt><enttypc Sync="FALSE">727</enttypc><enttypd>Each entity represents a spatial feature ( polyline) </enttypd><enttypds>Author-defined, based on analytical purpose and processing logic of this study, following ISO 19115 metadata guidance and ArcGIS Pro documentation standards.</enttypds></enttyp><attr xmlns=""><attrlabl Sync="TRUE">Travel_t</attrlabl><attalias Sync="TRUE">Travel_t</attalias><attrtype Sync="TRUE">Double</attrtype><attwidth Sync="TRUE">19</attwidth><atprecis Sync="TRUE">0</atprecis><attscale Sync="TRUE">0</attscale><attrdef>Estimated Travel Time: The time in minutes required to traverse the road segment, adjusted dynamically for flood impact.</attrdef><attrdefs>Formula for dry roads: Shape_Length / 83.33 5 km/h. Formula for flooded roads: Shape_Length / 8.33 0.5 km/h</attrdefs><attrdomv><rdom xmlns=""><rdommin>0.033236</rdommin><rdommax>10529.533019</rdommax></rdom></attrdomv></attr><attr xmlns=""><attrlabl>Is_flood30</attrlabl><attrdef>30-Year Flood Impact: A binary indicator (1 or 0) showing whether a road segment intersects with the HQ30 flood hazard zone.</attrdef><attrdefs>Derived via "Select by Location" intersecting the road layer with the RISIKOGEB_HQ30 extent .</attrdefs><attrtype>double</attrtype><attwidth>19</attwidth><attrdomv><rdom xmlns=""><rdommin>0</rdommin><rdommax>1</rdommax></rdom></attrdomv></attr><attr xmlns=""><attrlabl>Isflood100</attrlabl><attrdef>100-Year Flood Impact: A binary indicator (1 or 0) showing whether a road segment intersects with the HQ100 flood hazard zone.</attrdef><attrdefs>Derived via "Select by Location" intersecting the road layer with the RISIKOGEB_HQ100 extent.</attrdefs><attrtype>double</attrtype><attwidth>19</attwidth><attrdomv><rdom xmlns=""><rdommin>0</rdommin><rdommax>1</rdommax></rdom></attrdomv></attr></detailed></eainfo><mdDateSt Sync="TRUE">20260122</mdDateSt><mdContact xmlns=""><editorSource>external</editorSource><editorDigest>6045feea04197ffe86dafd59883a4fac69006bce</e